Summary: Allocate TLS expansion slots up front and expose them at %gs:0x1780
Category: cpu
Kind: workaround
Origin: crossover
  Version: 25.1.1
  CW-Hacks: 18756
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-25.1.1.tar.gz
  Files: dlls/ntdll/loader.c
  Changes: same code; placed just before FlsSlots is set up
  Note: Sikarugir 10.0_8 ships it: its x86_64 ntdll.dll has the "Darwin"
    string and a movq %rax, %gs:0x1780; a plain build's has neither
Upstream: differently (3a16aabb, Wine 10.5: GSBASE points at the TEB while
 PE code runs, so %gs:0x1780 is TEB->TlsExpansionSlots there)
Needed until: 10.5 (WineHQ 3a16aabb)
Why: Code that inlines TlsGetValue reads the TLS arrays through %gs:
 indexes 0-63 at %gs:0x1480 and the expansion array through the pointer at
 %gs:0x1780 (TEB->TlsExpansionSlots). In Wine 10.0 on macOS %gs is the
 pthread TSD, not the TEB, so both read libc's data. For 64-bit threads
 (not WoW64 ones), allocate the expansion array in loader_init and also
 store its pointer at %gs:0x1780; otherwise kernelbase allocates it on
 demand in TlsAlloc/TlsSetValue and never writes that %gs-relative copy.
 The first time, mark every free slot in the 64-entry TLS bitmap as used,
 so that every TlsAlloc afterwards hands out an expansion slot, which that
 pointer serves. Indexes 0-63 at %gs:0x1480 are still not mirrored.
 is_macos() checks wine_get_host_version for "Darwin".
Programs: none known; any 64-bit program or DLL that inlines TlsGetValue
Uncertain: which program CrossOver added it for (CW HACK 18756 isn't
 public). Programs that assume a TLS index below 64 (TLS_MINIMUM_AVAILABLE)
 get one of 64 or more.
Related: ntdll-peb-at-gs-0x60; the same cause (10.0's %gs is the pthread
 TSD), another TEB field
Status: 10.0: 2026-11-26: diff refreshed against the current stack, so it
 applies at fuzz 0 and needs no other patch as context; code unchanged.
 2026-11-25: on macfixes-10.0-build0 (local), TlsAlloc gave 65, 66, 67 and
 %gs:0x1780 was TEB->TlsExpansionSlots in two threads (patch review)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
@@ -4930,6 +4930,18 @@
 #endif
 }
 
+#if defined(__x86_64__) && !defined(__arm64ec__)
+extern void CDECL wine_get_host_version( const char **sysname, const char **release );
+
+static BOOL is_macos(void)
+{
+    const char *sysname;
+
+    wine_get_host_version( &sysname, NULL );
+    return !strcmp( sysname, "Darwin" );
+}
+#endif
+
 /******************************************************************
  *		loader_init
  *
@@ -5028,6 +5040,24 @@
 #endif
         wm = get_modref( NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->ImageBaseAddress );
     }
+
+#if defined(__x86_64__) && !defined(__arm64ec__)
+        if (is_macos() && !NtCurrentTeb()->WowTebOffset)
+        {
+            /* CW HACK 18756 */
+            /* Preallocate TlsExpansionSlots.  Otherwise, kernelbase will
+               allocate it on demand, but won't be able to do the Mac-specific poking to the
+               %gs-relative address. */
+            if (!NtCurrentTeb()->TlsExpansionSlots)
+                NtCurrentTeb()->TlsExpansionSlots = RtlAllocateHeap( GetProcessHeap(), HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY, 8 * sizeof(NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->TlsExpansionBitmapBits) * sizeof(void*) );
+            __asm__ volatile ("movq %0,%%gs:%c1"
+                              :
+                              : "r" (NtCurrentTeb()->TlsExpansionSlots), "n" (FIELD_OFFSET(TEB, TlsExpansionSlots)));
+
+            if (!attach_done) /* only the first time */
+                while (RtlFindClearBitsAndSet(NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->TlsBitmap, 1, 1) != ~0U);
+        }
+#endif
 
     NtCurrentTeb()->FlsSlots = fls_alloc_data();
 
